From d9a7f966b0b78a4f699ff7d708e332cdc47a27c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gandalf4212 <gandalf4212@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:09:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] D143: the renderer records RunCommandBuffer in OnEnter
 (its recorded draws were dropped)

---
 docs/decisions.md | 7 +++++++
 src/renderer.cpp  | 1 +
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/decisions.md b/docs/decisions.md
index cac7050..5b592ec 100644
--- a/docs/decisions.md
+++ b/docs/decisions.md
@@ -4526,3 +4526,10 @@ draw) came mostly from Present's packets: type-0 "packets" writing 4,100 to 16,3
 the old write position to the new segment, through stale ring data. The game now hooks it (src/native_x_renderer_abc.cpp).
 Here: a type-0 packet whose writes run past the register file is not a packet; the scan stops there (incomplete).
 Draws reload their constants from the shadow, which hid this; replays (non-draw gathers, D133) did not.
+
+## D143 — The renderer takes RunCommandBuffer's arguments: its recorded draws were dropped (2026-11-09)
+Logs 019/020: every replayed draw's state matches the command processor's (render state, fetch, programs, VS
+constants; PS c40-c43 differ only per tile, like the window offset), yet no jet and the near water flat grey. The
+renderer's OnEnter records the call it acts on (g_call) only for draws, resolves, Present and tiling; OnLeave returns
+when the tracked call is not g_call's. RunCommandBuffer was neither, so every draw D133 handed on was dropped before
+capture. RunCommandBuffer is now recorded in OnEnter.
diff --git a/src/renderer.cpp b/src/renderer.cpp
index 912150d..fa9545d 100644
--- a/src/renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/renderer.cpp
@@ -1956,6 +1956,7 @@ void OnEnter(Call call, PPCContext& ctx, uint8_t* base, bool nested) {
     case Call::kBeginTiling:
     case Call::kEndTiling:
     case Call::kQueryIssue:
+    case Call::kRunCommandBuffer:  // D143: its recorded draws (D133) are matched to this call in OnLeave
       break;
     default:
       if (!(Info(call).flags & kDraw)) return;
-- 
